  "factor_name": "Trend Efficiency Ratio 20d (Kaufman ER)",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "abs(close_t/close_{t-20} - 1) / (sum_{i=1..20} abs(ln(close_{t-i+1}/close_{t-i})) + 1e-12)",
    "description": "Kaufman efficiency ratio over 20 days: net 20d return magnitude divided by total 20d path length. High ER = smooth directional trend (small noise per unit of net move); low ER = choppy range. Cross-sectionally, smooth trends persist: high-ER assets tend to outperform over the following days (positive IC). Strict 20-of-20 window keeps the signal clean; partial windows (mp10) dilute ICIR below the gate."
  },
